### 4. Data Flow

```
User drops files in browser
        ↓
POST /upload → UploadService
  → validates files, saves to disk (storage/uploads/<project_uuid>/<uuid>_filename)
  → creates: Project, Document, ProcessingJob rows in PostgreSQL
  → dispatches: process_document.delay(job_id, document_id) to Celery via Redis
        ↓
Celery Worker: process_document task
  → ProcessingService: loads document, runs parser factory (PDF/DOCX/XLSX)
  → saves parsed_content (JSON page array) to Document row
  → marks status: uploaded → processing → parsed
  → dispatches: extract_requirements_task.delay(document_id, project_id)
        ↓
Celery Worker: extract_requirements_task
  → ExtractionService: reads raw file from disk
  → extracts full text (pdfplumber for PDFs, handles tables + prose separately)
  → sends full text to LLM in a single call with structured system prompt
  → parses JSON response, deduplicates by Jaccard similarity (>85% threshold)
  → saves rows to extracted_requirements table (FR-01, NFR-02, etc.)
        ↓
[Parallel RAG pipeline — see RAG_PIPELINE_FLOW.md]
  → chunk_document → ChunkingService (hierarchical)
  → semantic_chunk_document → SemanticChunkingService + classification
  → embed_document → EmbeddingPipeline (BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 → 384-dim vectors)
  → vectors stored in semantic_chunks table (Qdrant storage also prepared)
        ↓
Frontend polls GET /projects/{id}/status every 2s
  → shows real-time stage progress to user
        ↓
User navigates to Requirements panel
  → GET /projects/{id}/requirements → displays structured requirements
  → GET /search → semantic search over embedded chunks
```

