### 5. AI/ML Components

There are three distinct AI layers:

**LLM Extraction (primary)**
- Single-pass full-document extraction using Gemini 2.0 Flash (free default), Groq llama-3.3-70b, or Anthropic Claude Sonnet
- System prompt engineered to return a strict JSON schema with typed requirements
- Post-processing: JSON cleanup, Jaccard deduplication, auto-ID assignment (FR-01, NFR-02...)
- Provider is hot-swappable via `EXTRACTION_PROVIDER` env var — no code changes needed

**Semantic Embeddings (RAG core)**
- Model: `BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5` via `sentence-transformers` — 384-dimensional normalized dense vectors
- Model loaded once at worker startup (singleton), reused across calls
- Vectors stored in PostgreSQL `semantic_chunks.embedding_vector`; Qdrant support also scaffolded

**Classification (rule-based)**
- Chunk classifier using `classification/rules.py` and `classification/classifier.py`
- Categorizes chunks into 12 categories: functional, non_functional, ui_ux, integrations, security_compliance, data_validation, workflow_roles, infrastructure_deployment, risks_assumptions_dependencies, open_questions, out_of_scope, other

